id: pm-csv-mmi3
title: Route closed-status CSV imports through pm close with provenance reason
description: "pm-cli 2026.8.3 enforces governance.require_close_reason: pm create or pm update with a terminal closed status now hard-errors with close_reason_required (in 2026.7.29 it was silently auto-routed with a defaulted reason). pm-csv upsertCreate passes the CSV row status straight to pm create, so importing a row whose status is closed fails (atomic test: closed-status rows resume idempotently). Fix: create the item open, then transition via pm close with a factual provenance reason (the CSV carries no close-reason field), and align the upsertUpdate close reason with the same provenance instead of an invented outcome. Also bump the @unbrained/pm-cli pin to ^2026.8.3 / peer >=2026.8.3."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-03T22:04:53.566Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-03T22:05:01.847Z"
author: pi-agent
acceptance_criteria: "npm test passes under @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.3 including the atomic closed-status resume test; closed-status rows import as closed items via pm close with a factual provenance reason; no governance policy weakened; typecheck, build, coverage, changelog:check all pass"
body: ""
